# circleci_orbs (Data Source)

Lists CircleCI orbs, optionally scoped by namespace, name, visibility or certification. Every page of results is fetched.

Each entry carries only what the orb collection returns. The collection is genuinely thinner than the by-id route: there is no creation time, home page or usage count, and the namespace reference has an id but no name — so `namespace` here is derived from the qualified name rather than reported by the API. Use the `circleci_orb` data source when you need the full record for one orb.

Note that omitting `certified` is not the same as setting it to `false`: omitting it leaves the filter off entirely and lets the API choose, while `false` explicitly asks for uncertified orbs. Private orbs are not returned unless `visibility = "private"` is set.

~> **CircleCI Cloud only.** Orbs are served by the CircleCI v3 API, which CircleCI Server does not route to the public API service. Using this data source against a provider configured with `deployment = "server"` fails with an explicit error.

